+# KEDA External Scaler - Reference / Stub
+
+This directory contains a lightweight reference that demonstrates how to expose carbon estimates as Prometheus metrics or as a simple HTTP metric endpoint.
+
+Important:
+- KEDA supports a Prometheus trigger (recommended) which we already provide via `services/carbon_metrics_exporter_v2`.
+- Implementing a full KEDA External Scaler (external scalers that talk directly to the KEDA operator) requires following the KEDA External Scaler API and is vendor/cluster-specific; this stub is a starting point and exposes an HTTP endpoint with a derived metric for other components to scrape.
+
+Files:
+- app.py: simple HTTP endpoint returning derived metric (not full KEDA ExternalScaler protocol).
+- Dockerfile: builds image for hosting the endpoint.
+
+Recommended usage:
+- Use the Prometheus ScaledObject (ops/carbon/keda_prometheus_scaledobject.yaml) with `aegis_carbon_capacity` exported by `carbon_metrics_exporter_v2`.
+- If you need a full External Scaler implementation, use this stub as basis and replace endpoints to implement the required KEDA external scaler contract.
+
