+# Aegis Carbon Stack — Full Deploy Guide (one-click + manual steps)
+
+This document consolidates the deploy, verification and integration steps to make your Aegis platform fully carbon aware in staging.
+
+Prerequisites
+- kubectl configured for your staging cluster
+- docker (build & push) access to your registry
+- Postgres instance and connection string (DATABASE_URL)
+- (optional) ElectricityMap API key (ELECTRICITYMAP_API_KEY) or cloud provider carbon API access
+- Grafana admin API key (to import dashboards)
+
+Quick one‑click (recommended for staging)
+1. Export required env vars:
+   export DOCKER_REGISTRY=ghcr.io/yourorg
+   export DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:pass@host:5432/aegis"
+   export ELECTRICITYMAP_API_KEY="..."
+   export GITHUB_TOKEN="..."
+
+2. Run:
+   ./scripts/one_click_deploy.sh
+
+3. Run DB migration:
+   psql "${DATABASE_URL}" -f ops/db/migrations/0001_create_carbon_estimates.sql
+
+4. Update Prometheus scrape config:
+   - Add scrape jobs for:
+     - carbon/mock-power-emitter:9104
+     - monitoring/dcgm-exporter:9400 (GPU power)
+     - carbon/carbon-metrics-exporter:8000
+   Reload Prometheus.
+
+5. Import Grafana dashboard:
+   export GRAFANA_URL="https://grafana.example.com"
+   export GRAFANA_API_KEY="ey..."
+   ./scripts/import_grafana_dashboard.sh ops/monitoring/grafana/carbon_dashboard.json
+
+Smoke tests
+- scripts/test_carbon_stack.sh
+- tests/e2e_carbon/test_e2e_carbon.py (run in CI or locally with env vars)
+
+Worker integration
+- Add the post-job hook to your worker/job pipeline step:
+  PROV_PATH=/path/to/artifact.prov.json ARTIFACT_ID=job-123 DATABASE_URL=${DATABASE_URL} ./services/worker_hooks/prov_hook.sh
+
+Autoscaling & KEDA
+- We provide a Prometheus ScaledObject (ops/carbon/keda_prometheus_scaledobject.yaml) that uses aegis_carbon_capacity metric exported by carbon_metrics_exporter_v2.
+- Alternatively, adapt services/keda_external_scaler_stub as a starting point for a full external scaler implementation.
+
+Budget enforcement
+- Configure ops/carbon/carbon_budgets.json with team budgets.
+- The enforcer cronjob will create GitHub issues when budgets are exceeded (ensure GITHUB_TOKEN secret present).
+
+Security & production hardening
+- Run a security review of endpoints, secure secrets using Vault, enable TLS/mTLS for internal services, enable network policies, and run SBOM & image signing.
+
+Support
+- If you want, I can generate a fully templated Helm chart (values.yml) for the carbon stack tailored to your cloud provider and CI environment.
+
